WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.670
Hey everyone, this is Jared, a creator
here at Wisecrack. Today we have a special

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:11.520
episode about a series that everyone’s going
crazy for: Fallout. Let's set the scene:

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.780
"What is this 'fallout' anyhow?"

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.100
The Fallout series takes place around the
23rd century, in an alternate reality where

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:24.430
the culture of the 1950s just wouldn’t die,
but most of humanity does. In this world,

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:28.509
the cold war mentality was prevalent right
until the bitter end. After nations began

00:00:28.509 --> 00:00:33.000
to run out of oil in the 2050’s, the world
plunged into a global conflict that ended

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.539
in 2077 when the then-nuclear powers decided
to launch their arsenals at each other, enveloping

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:42.809
the world into a new dark age.
Apocalyptic fiction is a goldmine of philosophical

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:49.649
analysis- and Fallout is no different. Welcome
to this special episode on The Philosophy of Fallout.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:55.859
In our first section, we’ll be talking about
how society, culture and propaganda can convince

00:00:55.859 --> 00:01:01.780
us to do really, really stupid things. Okay
so we know that a nuclear war completely devastated

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:06.200
Earth, but one of the more fascinating questions
is how did it get there?

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.500
In the alternate reality, fascination with
atomic power proliferated during the mid 20th

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.640
century, and was never offset by the invention
of the transistor – you know, those little

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.570
electrical parts that led to the radio, computer,
and the smartphone you’re probably watching

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:23.440
this video on. As a result, the prewar society
of Fallout is technologically advanced like

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.640
our own, but in a slightly different way.
Technology is big, and bulky, and the computers

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:35.120
are primitive compared to our own. On the
other hand, they have badass power armor and

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.300
laser guns, so society as a whole probably
didn’t miss the advent of Minecraft that much.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.840
The Wasteland, the general term for the nightmare

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.450
landscape that pervades the game, is filled
with reminders of the sheer optimism of the

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.740
pre-war world. It was the age of atomic energy,
where our greatest dreams could be accomplished

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:54.720
with a little ingenuity and maybe a few giant
anti-communist death robots

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.760
"Death is preferable alternative to communism."

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.600
Nowhere is this optimism more apparent than
in the vaults themselves.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.700
Even when nuclear

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:08.460
annihilation seems imminent, the remnant Vault
posters maintain a certain cheeriness.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.640
Now, let’s ignore the fact that many of
the vaults were really just a cover for the

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.760
government to concoct insane experiments on
its residents.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.680
"Haha, Garryyyy..."

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.230
The Vaults are a testament to the human power
of cognitive dissonance. The possibility of

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:26.670
being locked in an underground bunker for
an indeterminate amount of time is advertised

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:31.569
as an exciting foray, where you can meet new
friends and raise a family. The vaults are

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:37.040
a callback to the luxury bomb shelters of
the Cold War era - yes, they really existed.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.989
These mental gymnastics were taken up by German-American philosopher Herbert Marcuse during the height

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:47.379
of the Cold War. He argued that these pleasant
appearances plastered over modern day nightmares

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:51.460
were a testament to the ability of modern
society to destroy criticism.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:58.240
"You know how bad sunburn can feel. The atomic bomb blast could burn you worse than a terrible sunburn."

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.680
In other words, capitalism is so damn good at

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:06.420
marketing, it makes even the worst shit in
the world just seem “dandy.” He even cites

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:11.689
the real life “deluxe fallout shelter,”
replete with televisions, lounge chairs and

00:03:11.689 --> 00:03:16.790
Scrabble boards as the ultimate example of
the “obscene merger” between appearance

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:23.000
and reality- between a cozy luxury getaway,
and a situation that unilaterally sucks balls.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.360
This disparity between appearance and reality

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:30.499
is what drives the humor of Fallout. We are
constantly confronted with contrary images:

00:03:30.499 --> 00:03:35.180
the quaint and cheery Leave-it-to-Beaver-esque
culture and the hellscape it’s set in. In

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.249
addition to the vaults, this can be observed
in the game’s radio stations that serenade

00:03:39.249 --> 00:03:44.249
the Wasteland with chipper jazz tunes as the
player fends off the crazed irradiated remnants

00:03:44.249 --> 00:03:45.380
of the human race

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.220
"Hellooooo, Capitol Wasteland!"

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.180
The use of the song
“I Don’t Want to Set the World on Fire,”

00:03:52.189 --> 00:03:56.669
used prominently in the game’s trailer,
plays off of the song’s innocent romanticism

00:03:56.669 --> 00:04:00.239
with the imagery of the burnt out remains
of Washington DC.

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:09.529
And, you know, the world was literally set
on fire. Other songs, like Cole Porter’s

00:04:09.529 --> 00:04:14.609
upbeat “Anything Goes,” a song about the
lax morals of modern society, is a nod to

00:04:14.609 --> 00:04:21.299
the absolute anarchy of the Wasteland, where
in addition to “exposed women’s stocking,”

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:23.810
cannibalism is also fair game.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:28.680
These marriages between positive and negative,
happy and sad, dream and nightmare aren’t

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:33.250
just comedic. It’s the mechanism in which
we as a society are constantly celebrating

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:39.060
the same culture and technology that consistently
puts us at the brink of total annihilation.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:43.240
We may laugh at this ironic play of elements,
but we can also view it as a criticism of

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.830
government propaganda.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:48.979
Marcuse argued that we are living in an age
of “one-dimensional thought,” enabled

00:04:48.979 --> 00:04:54.330
by the merging of positive and negative, where
rationality and technology can only go one

00:04:54.330 --> 00:05:01.490
way - forward. In other words- we are told
that technology is always good. Always. So

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:05.470
while society is free to debate about the
best way to bring order to the Wasteland or

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:06.400
kill Communists

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:10.620
"Democracy is truth. Communism is a lie."

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.660
there is no room “negative thought” or ideas

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.780
that undermine the one-dimensional, inane
positivity of society.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.810
This is perhaps most clear at the beginning of Fallout 3, where

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:26.120
the player is literally trapped at their own
birthday party until they have a sufficient

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.270
amount of fun.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:32.360
Another component of “making everyone A-OK
with our twisted reality” is simply by making

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:36.819
them too happy to care.
This leads us to The Enclave. The Enclave

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:41.940
is what’s left of the United States government
that want to purge the Wasteland of, well,

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:47.740
everybody. We learn that John Henry Eden,
the president of “The United States” is a computer.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.060
"Ahh, face to face at last."

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:54.620
As if an actual computer trying
to kill everybody wasn’t enough to demonstrate

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.680
the dangers of one-dimensional thinking, Eden
understands the

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:02.400
importance of fun and leisure in an obedient
society. In one of his radio addresses to

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:07.580
the Wasteland, Eden praises the virtue of
baseball as some savior to the American dream:

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:13.580
"I am referring, of course, to our great national pastime: baseball.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:22.140
That's right, America. Before we were devastated by atomic war, each state had its own professional baseball team.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:28.780
Their purpose: to make you, dear America, revel in the joys of sport and sunshine.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:35.560
Put your faith in John Henry Eden, great America, and baseball will live again."

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:40.160
The comfort and recreation that John Henry
Eden is trying to revive are hallmarks of

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:45.759
the prewar society. The Wasteland is littered
with reminders of our own excess: leisure

00:06:45.759 --> 00:06:50.349
suits, magazines, televisions. We’re even
confronted with a gang that mistakenly thinks

00:06:50.349 --> 00:06:52.780
that Elvis Presley is some kind of deity.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:00.180
These comforts provide us as an easy way to

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:04.840
cope with the horrific reality around us.
Eden is trying to resurrect the same kind

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:08.849
of distracted society that got us in
this mess in the first place. A society that

00:07:08.849 --> 00:07:13.080
probably wouldn’t mind if he tried to kill
them all, because, well, he’s still totally trying

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:20.979
to do that too.
From the Great War that decimated the world,

00:07:20.979 --> 00:07:24.729
to the secret government experiments that
created the Super Mutants that are now trying

00:07:24.729 --> 00:07:29.770
to kill you; we’re constantly reminded of
technology run amok. In Fallout, as in real

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:34.939
life, technology is a double edged sword-
both good guy and bad guy.

00:07:34.939 --> 00:07:39.229
So when we, as players, are confronted with
choices about technology, the game presents

00:07:39.229 --> 00:07:42.990
us with a series of moral dilemmas.
Should technology be used to provide clean

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:48.039
water for the people of the Wasteland, or
unleash a devastating virus to purify

00:07:48.039 --> 00:07:52.300
it of its violence and corruption?
Who should gain control of Mr. House’s robotic

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:56.780
army in the battle over the fate of New Vegas?
These questions, for the thoughtful player,

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:00.240
can be quite troublesome.
The idea that humans can’t handle technology

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:05.259
is really old. Fallout draws inspiration from
the Greek myth of Phaethon, the son of the

00:08:05.259 --> 00:08:10.259
sun-god Helios. Phaethon, being the brash
child he was, decided to take his dad’s

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.060
ride for a spin. But unlike your dad’s Porsche

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:16.480
"Porsche: there is no substitute."

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:21.610
Helios’ ride was a chariot that
carried the actual sun across the sky. It

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:26.710
went exactly as you’d expect, with Phaethon
pretty much ruining everything –and burning

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:31.729
up huge portions of the Earth. In New Vegas,
the giant solar plant capable of harnessing

00:08:31.729 --> 00:08:37.550
(pun intended) the sun’s energy is called
Helios One. And like Sun-god Jr., the player

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:42.329
can gleefully take the sun’s destructive
power for a joy ride and slaughter thousands

00:08:42.329 --> 00:08:45.529
of NCR soldiers.
One response to this technological dilemma

00:08:45.529 --> 00:08:50.380
is the Brotherhood of Steel, the secretive
order of power-armor clad badasses who roam

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:55.610
the Wasteland looking for long lost technology.
Like post-apocalyptic hoarders, the Brotherhood

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:59.570
stashes their technology in heavily armored
bases to make sure that it doesn’t fall

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:02.180
into the wrong hands - the wrong hands, of
course, being

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:06.660
anybody but them. The Brotherhood is so insistent
that nobody can be trusted with technology

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:11.649
but themselves that they will go to war with
any faction possessing advanced tech.

00:09:11.649 --> 00:09:15.410
Perhaps the Brotherhood is right that we can’t
be trusted with technology, but if so, it’s

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:17.990
probably also true that they shouldn’t be
trusted either.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:22.470
The other response to technology is seen in
Caesar’s legion, who swears off technology

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:26.430
except the kind that enables its user to kill
better. But unlike the Brotherhood who thinks

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:30.899
technology is inherently dangerous, Caesar
believes that technology makes people weak

00:09:30.899 --> 00:09:34.120
and dependent.
Even without technology, Caesar’s legion

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:39.410
manages to do plenty of wrong-doing. The brutal,
totalitarian state doesn’t need super computers

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:43.019
or power armors to make everyone’s live
a living hell. So maybe technology isn’t

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.360
to blame after all.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.280
The citizens of the Wasteland come together

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:54.500
to create various forms of governments, from
cruel tyranny fueled slavery, to liberal

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:59.160
democracies, to uh, whatever this is
Aside from illustrating political theories

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:03.990
from the days of yore, Fallout also does a
pretty good job of explaining modern theories

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:07.899
about international relations.
In New Vegas, Caesar wants to unite all of

00:10:07.899 --> 00:10:13.220
humanity under his banner in a dystopian nightmare
where everyone is a slave and Roman cosplayer.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:18.000
While Caesar’s Legion is superficially modeled
after the Roman Empire, the actual foreign

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:23.430
policy of Caesar is alive and well today.
Caesar thinks that peace comes through security

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:28.420
and doesn’t believe that peace is attainable
until his Legion is the only dominant faction

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:33.230
in the Wasteland, if not the only faction
at all. In international relations, we call

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:37.990
this the “hegemonic stability theory,” which
believes that superpowers scare the living

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:41.240
hell out of everyone else and they all, for
the most part, behave.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.860
"America, f*ck yeah!"

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:49.360
To an extent, it works in the game. Traders
prefer to trade in Legion territory because

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:53.620
it’s safer. Raiders have been eliminated
and everyone is terrified to break the law.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:57.920
Traders in NCR territory, however, always
have to be on alert for raiders and other

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.970
small factions.
Every faction in Fallout is essentially trying

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:05.630
to become the local hegemon, the international
equivalent of the playground bully, by putting

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:09.339
other factions in their place and vying for
power. And it goes without saying that if

00:11:09.339 --> 00:11:14.220
Caesar eliminated the NCR and other factions,
there would be some sort of “peace” on

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.400
the Wasteland.
If you’re not looking to enslave the whole

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:20.640
world, there are other options available.
In many situations, a balance of power among

00:11:20.649 --> 00:11:26.529
factions makes war too costly. If the NCR
hasn’t invaded New Vegas to annex it, it’s

00:11:26.529 --> 00:11:30.220
not because they’re a bunch of outstanding
citizens, but because the cost would simply

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:34.790
be too high. The Boomers understand this,
and like a post-apocalyptic Switzerland, have

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:39.110
only managed to stay out of everyone’s business
by protecting their borders with a constant

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:42.570
barrage of artillery fire.
For those who ascribe to a “realist” model

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:47.350
of international relations, each faction or
state is only out to save their own hide,

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:51.690
and power is a zero-sum game. The only way
to ensure security is to make sure you have

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:56.829
more vertibirds than the next guy. Peace is
only achieved by uncertain ceasefires between,

00:11:56.829 --> 00:12:03.070
say, the NCR and the Enclave. Alliances are
fleeting, and only exist to combat more powerful,

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.490
and dangerous, factions. Now, whether or not
this works is debatable. Even in the real

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:10.300
world, lots of wars are fought over who gets
to be in charge.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:13.160
"America, f*ck yeah!"

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.180
It precludes the ability

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:18.389
of factions to work together and truly trust
each other, and isn’t that what launched

00:12:18.389 --> 00:12:20.829
us into nuclear holocaust in the first place?

00:12:20.829 --> 00:12:25.649
The stakes of diplomatic relationships in
Fallout are always REALLY high. Namely because

00:12:25.649 --> 00:12:29.980
every single issue is caught in a life and
death struggle for the soul of humanity.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.649
But how far are you willing to go to maintain
your security?

00:12:32.649 --> 00:12:37.540
Should the NCR resort to bullying, tolerate
corruption, and make alliances with not-so-scrupulous

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:42.029
figures to maintain the peace and expand their
power, all in the name of democracy? In Fallout

00:12:42.029 --> 00:12:47.009
3, how far will you go to bring clean water
to the Wasteland? Should you, as a player,

00:12:47.009 --> 00:12:50.420
murder every obstacle, or seek the diplomatic
approach?

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:54.519
Assuming you haven’t decided to play the
game in the most evil way possible, many make

00:12:54.519 --> 00:13:00.160
a choice to support whoever is “right.”
Maybe you believe that the NCR, while flawed,

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.759
is the kind of democracy that the world needs.
Or maybe you think technology needs to be

00:13:03.759 --> 00:13:06.420
taken from the irresponsible actors who possess it.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:11.220
The problem with “security logic,” according
to some philosophers, is its totalizing logic.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:15.410
Daniel Callahan argues that there is no limit
in the amount of terrible, grotesque things

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:17.500
we are willing to do in the name of survival.

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:19.540
Or, in the words of ol’ Ben Franklin “Those

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.779
who surrender freedom for security will not
have, nor

00:13:22.779 --> 00:13:26.149
do they deserve, either one.”
The point is not lost on Enclave President

00:13:26.149 --> 00:13:28.480
John Henry Eden, who declares on radio:

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:30.160
"The question has been raised,

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.920
I know, as to just how I came to be elected.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:41.560
Unfortunately, in the interest of national security, I'm
not at liberty to discuss the details of the election."

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:46.100
The Enclave will go so far to save the
“real” humanity that they will exterminate all the

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:50.420
mutated riff raff that threatens them.
A similar despotism is seen in New Vegas,

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:55.069
though a little less genocidal. If you work
for Mr. House in New Vegas until the conclusion,

00:13:55.069 --> 00:13:59.459
you’ll trigger an ending the looks like
this: “Mr. House continued to run New Vegas

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:06.960
his way, a despotic vision of pre-War glory.
The streets were orderly, efficient, cold.”

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:10.870
In other words, the chaos of the Wasteland
could be tamed after all, but only at the

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:15.990
expense of personal freedoms and democracy.
Mr. House is explicit in his distaste for

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:21.230
freedom, saying “Nothing to impede progress.
If you want to see the fate of democracies,

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:28.449
look out the windows. But autocracy?
Firm control in the hands of a technological

00:14:28.449 --> 00:14:33.550
and economic visionary? Yes, that Vegas shall have.”

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:39.149
In actual history, we see security as a constant
theme among dictators. Crises are manufactured,

00:14:39.149 --> 00:14:44.529
and threats exaggerated to justify more police
and more repressive laws. In the world of

00:14:44.529 --> 00:14:47.400
Fallout, there are no shortages of these crises
to exploit.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:54.340
One of the most fascinating elements of
the Fallout series is its constant interrogation

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:58.459
of human society and government. The game’s
refrain that “War never changes” might

00:14:58.459 --> 00:15:03.190
as well say “humanity never changes.”
After all, aside from the feral ghouls and

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:08.410
super mutants, the scariest part of the Wasteland
is a rehashing of our own regrettable history:

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:14.680
slavery obsessed Romans, Orwellian dictatorships,
and genocidal governments. History, it seems,

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:16.480
does repeat itself.

